NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000

# T8 — WebRTC ICE server configuration (see lib/webrtc/config.ts for the
# full explanation). All optional; a public Google STUN server is used by
# default for local development if NEXT_PUBLIC_WEBRTC_STUN_URL is unset.
# TURN is NOT configured out of the box — this project has no TURN
# service, and long-lived credentials in a NEXT_PUBLIC_* var are not a
# safe production pattern regardless. Without TURN, calls between peers
# on restrictive/symmetric NATs may fail to connect P2P — a known,
# documented limitation, not something T8 claims to solve.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WEBRTC_STUN_URL=stun:stun.l.google.com:19302
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WEBRTC_TURN_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WEBRTC_TURN_USERNAME=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WEBRTC_TURN_CREDENTIAL=
